Valuable Comments:
I liked how organized this course was. All of the lecture notes and anticipated due dates were posted on his website at the beginning of the year. Before tests there would also be study questions that were similar to the content on the exam, and there was also quite a bit of extra credit. If you put in the effort, you'd do well in this class. I feel like the homework assignments were constructed well and really helped me grow as a coder. I genuinely enjoyed this class, and I'm glad I took it despite it being outside of my intended major. | This professor is kind of good he knows what he is doing but his homework's are hard asf he thinks you are a professional coder given that it's an intro level class and not part of computer science major if you are planning to major in computer science do not take this class because this class weeds out a lot of people trying to get into CS without any prior knowledge of coding his answers are ambiguous. | The course was a great introduction to the computer science field, and even has inspired me to try double majoring with it and my current Applied Math major. The structure of the homeworks/labs was probably the most valuable part of the course, as it was stimulating at times while acting as a great way to develop your own understanding of the material. | Very great introduction to programming.  Feel more confidant going into my other CS courses after having no previous experience in computer science or coding.  
